# Packages strapd pulls in outside strapd-base.packages, hardware-conditional
# drivers, kernels, and the pieces install/* installs directly. The ISO builder
# reads this so they are available offline.
#
# AUR entries are in strapd-aur.packages.
#
# Some hardware packages resolve nowhere and are deliberately not listed: the
# T2 MacBook set (apple-bcm-firmware, apple-t2-audio-config, linux-t2,
# linux-t2-headers, t2fanrd), which lives in the t2linux repo strapd does not
# add, and linux-ptl, linux-ptl-headers, intel-ipu7-camera and
# dell-xps-touchpad-haptics, which have no source at all.
#
# install/hardware/apple/fix-t2.sh, intel/ptl-kernel.sh, intel/ipu7-camera.sh
# and dell-xps-touchpad-haptics.sh still ask for those by name, so on the
# machines they detect the install fails loudly rather than skipping in
# silence. That is deliberate: a list entry resolving to nothing would paper
# over it.

autoconf-archive
base
base-devel
broadcom-wl
btrfs-progs
dkms
egl-wayland
gst-plugin-pipewire
gtk4-layer-shell
libpulse
intel-lpmd
intel-media-driver
libva-intel-driver
libva-nvidia-driver
limine
linux
linux-firmware
linux-headers
nvidia-open-dkms
nvidia-utils
lib32-nvidia-utils
pipewire
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-jack
pipewire-pulse
qt6-wayland
snapper
sof-firmware
thermald
webp-pixbuf-loader
zram-generator

# Intel encoding processing
libvpl
vpl-gpu-rt

# Vulkan drivers (auto-detected by hardware)
vulkan-intel
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-asahi

# Surface laptop support packages
linux-firmware-marvell

# Speaker tunings (LV2 limiter every tuning ends in)
lsp-plugins-lv2

# Framework 16
